
MoM – Today’s Client Meeting

Key Discussion Points

* Architecture: Reuse and enhance existing tables/components wherever functionality overlaps; avoid creating duplicate tables and functionality.
* ToE & Tickets: Use the existing List + Item structure for ticket/support workflows and explore reusable list-level templates.
* PR & Environments: Define a clear Local → Remote Dev → Staging → Production flow with human approval gates and automated GitHub PR testing.
* LangGraph/LangSmith: Start scaffolding reusable graphs, subgraphs and nodes, with LangSmith supporting agent monitoring/evaluation and knowledge-gap workflows.
* Knowledge Base: Implement hierarchical and user-specific permissions at Knowledge Base → Node → Article levels, including CRUD/publish/archive permissions.
* Shared Entity Model: Reduce junction-table sprawl and create reusable shared components such as comments, notes, history, QA, notifications, etc.
* Assets & Files: Establish a common Asset → File → File Version structure that can be reused across Goals, Knowledge Articles and other entities.
* Cleanup: During migration, identify and remove dead code, unused tables and obsolete POC functionality.
* Repository Consolidation: Evaluate consolidation/integration of the Oakbridge and Databricks repositories to avoid manual code/SQL copying and reduce repository sprawl.

Next Steps

* Team to review the architecture and existing implementation.
* Prepare recommendations for repository strategy, shared entities, permissions, migration, and PR/staging process.
* Discuss and validate the proposed approach in the next follow-up meeting.
